# Line endings: the repository stores text with LF, and the working tree uses LF too, whatever
# core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows and the windows-latest runners default it to true). The
# JSON Lines fixtures and the protocol's golden fixtures are compared byte for byte, the
# daemon talks to its CLIs in LF-separated JSON Lines, and android/gradlew is a shell script.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF in the working tree (cmd.exe misreads labels and line
# continuations in LF batch files); the repository still stores LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.tzst binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
